Subject: [PATCH] rtl8192cd-rtl8197f: the AC8 driver selects DRIVER_11AC_SUPPORT

hostapd is built with CONFIG_IEEE80211AC only when a selected Wi-Fi
driver sets DRIVER_11AC_SUPPORT, as the mac80211 and mt76 11ac drivers
do.  kmod-rtl8192cd-rtl8197f-ac8 drives the RTL8812F (802.11ac) but did
not, so wpad-basic-mbedtls rejected the VHT80 configuration of the
5 GHz radio on the AC8 ("unknown configuration item 'vht_oper_chwidth'",
"hostapd.add_iface failed") and the access point never came up.

---
--- a/package/kernel/rtl8192cd-rtl8197f/Makefile
+++ b/package/kernel/rtl8192cd-rtl8197f/Makefile
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@
 define KernelPackage/rtl8192cd-rtl8197f-ac8
 $(call KernelPackage/rtl8192cd-rtl8197f/Default)
   TITLE:=RTL8197FH + RTL8812F WLAN driver for Tenda AC8 (cfg80211)
-  DEPENDS+= +kmod-cfg80211
+  DEPENDS+= +kmod-cfg80211 +@DRIVER_11AC_SUPPORT
   VARIANT:=ac8
   CONFLICTS:=kmod-rtl8192cd-rtl8197f-mw5 kmod-rtl8192cd-rtl8197f-rd05 kmod-rtl8192cd-rtl8197f-ac23
 endef
